WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
[DRAMATIC MUSIC]

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.840
 What's up, everybody?

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.880
I'm Langston Belton.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.610
And I am joined by the
cast and creative team

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.660
of Marvel Studios' Loki.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.600
Hello, everyone.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.170
All right, let's get into it.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.340
So at the end of episode
one, we find out that there

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.090
are multiple Lokis out there.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.870
So, Tom, what was
it like approaching

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.520
this role with that knowledge?

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.100
 Well, you know, we contain
multitudes, as the saying goes.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.150
I found there's so many
multifaceted aspects

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:40.030
of his character,
which often exist

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.350
within him, either in
concert or in conflict.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.660
And that's part of the
pleasure I have in playing him.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.400
And then to have the interior
multiplicity externalized

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.790
was thrilling.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.590
 Ah.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:55.420
So for the rest of
you, what was it

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.560
like building a brand-new series
around a character like Loki

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.660
that the fans already
know and love?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.460
 Tom is a Loki encyclopedia.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.890
And we kind of came
up with this idea,

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.540
and I was like, we
should do Loki school.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.300
And he basically like spoke
to all my heads of department

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.220
and did, like, a Loki lecture.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.440
 Meeting with him, and
him kind of walking me

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.230
through over the course
of a few days, kind

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:20.860
of the whole mythology and
explaining his character

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.050
and letting me kind
of ask questions.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:27.560
And I think that stuff really
helped within our dynamic

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.170
once we started filming.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:32.630
 Now there are some amazing
new characters in this series,

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:33.430
as well.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.010
Can you please tell us a little
bit about your characters?

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.970
 My character-- she is
a hunter, Hunter B-15.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:41.570
And she works for the TVA.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.370
She's pretty rigid.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.670
[LAUGHS] She's a little cheeky,
too, and a little salty.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:51.940
 I play Ravonna Renslayer,
who is a judge in the TVA.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:52.990
She's worked her way up.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.980
She had a history as a
hunter, a more military role,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.170
like Wunmi's character.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.840
And she came up from that to
be sort of one of the most

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.110
powerful judges in the
TVA who reports directly

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.150
to the Time-Keepers,
who are sort

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.460
of the all-seeing
overlords of time.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:13.120
 Oh, nice And, Owen,
your character, Mobius,

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.910
goes out of his way to
enlist the help of Loki.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.970
So what's on Mobius's mind?

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:22.330
 Well, you know,
nothing much, just

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.160
the fate of the whole universe.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.270
Uh-- [LAUGHS]

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.940
 Let's talk about
the whole universe.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.090
If there are variant
versions of all of you

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.710
out there across
various timelines,

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.110
what do you think
they're up to right now?

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:39.520
 [LAUGHS] Oh, my gosh.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.495
I don't know.

00:02:40.495 --> 00:02:42.220
Variant versions of me.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.480
 There are.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:52.600
And some are, you know, some
are very quiet and well-behaved,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.220
and some are more mischievous.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.450
 I suppose there's a version
of me in some alternate reality

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.430
who didn't get cast as Loki.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.480
A teacher?

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.810
Is he a gardener?

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:03.610
No.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.765
I'd be a terrible gardener.

00:03:04.765 --> 00:03:06.670
I just don't have it in the DNA.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.610
 There's probably ballet
Gugu and painter Gugu.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:13.930
 Oh, an archaeologist.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.560
Or a volcanic researcher.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.720
Those are all things I wanted
to do when I was a kid.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.650
 In episode one, we get a
tour of the incredible TVA

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.670
headquarters.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:28.330
What was it like creating a
brand-new location for the MCU?

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.620
 I think, for me,
the exciting thing

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.680
in creating the TVA is this
organization that exists

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.400
outside of space and time.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.580
So it's kind of like
Vegas in a way that--

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.390
it's not on a planet.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.190
There's no sun.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.060
It's in this unknowable
kind of place.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.160
And the comic books have
these amazing images of, like,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.560
these desks stretching
off into infinity, which

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.150
is definitely something
we took to our designer

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.500
and were inspired by.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.320
 We had to define
what that power set is.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.990
There were certainly just
a lot of time travel rule

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.950
defining that we had to do.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:04:01.870
But ultimately, very exciting to
take the most powerful arguably

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.470
magical organization that
you could possibly conceive,

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.290
and then make them as
boring as possible.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.800
Just purely
bureaucratic paperwork.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.840
 Well, some people
find paperwork exciting.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.990
To each their own, right?

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.790
Well, all right.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:16.590
I'm sorry.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.760
I got to put you on the spot.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.240
What are you most excited for
fans to see in this series?

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.290
 I mean, the whole thing.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.810
It's a whole new world.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:30.130
And it just opens you
up to different ideas,

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.310
and about good and bad,
and right and wrong,

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:34.570
and hero villain.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:40.420
 I am most excited for fans to
see what happens to Loki when

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.400
he has nowhere left to run.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.310
And he can't delude
himself anymore.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.140
And I'll stop talking,
otherwise I'll say too much.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.520
 Well, we are all very
excited to see what comes next.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.500
Thank you all so
much for joining me.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.550
And all of you out there, don't
miss Marvel Studios' Loki,

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.250
with new episodes
streaming every Wednesday

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.200
exclusively on Disney+.

